    "https://brocku.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/brocku_careers/job/St-Catharines-Main-Campus/Administrative-Assistant-3_JR-1025393": {
      "title": "Administrative Assistant - Faculty of Mathematics and Science",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-24\nPosted: Posted Today\nFull time\n\nBrock University is located on the traditional territory of the Haudenosaunee and Anishinaabe peoples, many of whom continue to live and work here today. This territory is covered by the Upper Canada Treaties and is within the land protected by the Dish with One Spoon Wampum Agreement.  We are one of Canada’s outstanding comprehensive universities, where excellence and innovation thrive! Brock has been proudly recognized as a Hamilton-Niagara Top Employer for eight consecutive years. Brock continues to earn recognition as one of Canada’s Best Employers and one of Canada’s Best Employers for Diversity in 2026. For the second consecutive year, Forbes, in partnership with Statista, also named Brock one of Canada’s Top Employers for Company Culture. At Brock, you will find a welcoming, inclusive community and an exciting range of meaningful career opportunities. Ignite new possibilities for your career. Break through at Brock. Post End Date: October 5, 2026 at 11:59 PM This job advertisement is to fill an existing vacancy in the OSSTF (Employee Group) About the Role:   Reporting to the Faculty Service Manager, the Administrative Assistant provides frontline service and comprehensive administrative support to faculty leadership, staff, and students. The incumbent ensures smooth day-to-day operations, effective communication, and administrative support for departmental activities. The incumbent acts as the first point of contact, addresses inquiries, supports administrative and operational processes, and assists with logistics while maintaining compliance with institutional standards   The Administrative Assistant will:   Provide day-to-day administrative assistance to academic leadership and faculty members; Coordinate communications, prepare documents and correspondence, and support scheduling needs; Act as a liaison between departments, and other units to facilitate effective administrative supports; Provide data entry and expense transactions processing, including reimbursements and purchasing records; Ensure timely and accurate recording of all financial transactions, submitting Finance/AP or through financial systems as appropriate; Review and process faculty and departmental travel and expense reports, including submissions related to meetings, conferences, luncheons, events, and recruitment activities; Maintain records, filing systems, tracking, and databases in accordance with privacy guidelines; Support student award processes and maintain accurate filing systems and databases;  Assist with postings and contracts in Workday (e.g., TAs, RAs, overloads), ensuring compliance with collective agreements; Serve as the first point of contact for faculty, staff, and students, responding to inquiries and processing frequent requests; Manage generic email accounts, answer general questions, redirect inquiries, and provide accurate information to ensure timely communication; Schedule department and committee meetings, prepare agendas, and record minutes;  Plan and manage logistics for events, workshops, colloquia, and conferences hosted by the program, including guest speakers, student research days, high school visits, and alumni events.   undefined Key Skills and Experience:  Diploma or degree in a related discipline. The equivalent combination of education and experience would be considered; Experience in administrative or office support role; Proficiency with computer systems and software applications; Ability and willingness to learn and adapt to emerging technologies, including AI tools and platforms; Ability to maintain accurate records, including file retention and tracking; Excellent writing, grammar, editing, and proofreading skills; Promotes and embodies inclusivity and respect within the workplace and the broader community; Excellent communication and interpersonal skills; Ability to provide responsive and professional support to faculty, staff, and students; Works cooperatively with colleagues to achieve departmental goals; Strong organizational and time-management skills with attention to detail; Ability to maintain precise records and manages complex schedules effectively; Responds effectively to changing priorities and peak workload periods; and   Salary and Benefit Information Job Grade H, Salary Scale ($46,099 - $63,950)* This position includes full comprehensive benefits including tuition waiver. This position will be required to work on site 5 days per week.  This position is included in the Ontario Secondary School Teachers Federation (OSSTF) Union and: Salary is therefore determined by the OSSTF Collective agreement. * New members shall be placed on the salary grid at the entry level. * It is Brock University’s policy to give first consideration to qualified internal Brock University OSSTF applicants. We are committed to offering flexible work arrangements where possible as outlined in our Flexible Work Arrangement Policy . As a student-centered organization, all employees are required to work on campus as needed.   Brock University is committed to creating a respectful and equitable workplace. We strive to foster a culture of diversity and inclusion in our work and learning environments. We welcome applications from all qualified individuals and actively encourage applications from women, people with disabilities, members of the 2SLGBTQIA+ community, Indigenous Peoples, people who identify as Black, African and/or Caribbean, as racialized and/or as from ethnic and cultural minority groups, and other underrepresented demographic groups at Brock and in the Niagara region. Brock also recognizes intersectionality and the interconnected identities, histories, and experiences of these aforementioned groups .   We are committed to inclusive and barrier-free recruitment, and we accommodat e the needs of applicants throughout all stages of the recruitment process, as outlined in our Employment Accommodation Policy and consistent with the requirements of the Ontario Human Rights Code . Please contact talent@brocku.ca   if you require a disability related accommodation so we can ensure you r participation needs are met.   Brock University does not use AI Technology at any stage of the recruitment process.   We appreciate all applications received . C andidates that are selected for an interview will be contacted.   Learn more about Brock University by visiting www.brocku.ca ."
    },
    "https://brocku.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/brocku_careers/job/St-Catharines-Main-Campus/Administrative-Coordinator_JR-1025341": {
      "title": "Administrative Coordinator",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-25\nPosted: Posted Today\nFull time\n\nBrock University is located on the traditional territory of the Haudenosaunee and Anishinaabe peoples, many of whom continue to live and work here today. This territory is covered by the Upper Canada Treaties and is within the land protected by the Dish with One Spoon Wampum Agreement.  We are one of Canada’s outstanding comprehensive universities, where excellence and innovation thrive! Brock has been proudly recognized as a Hamilton-Niagara Top Employer for eight consecutive years. Brock continues to earn recognition as one of Canada’s Best Employers and one of Canada’s Best Employers for Diversity in 2026. For the second consecutive year, Forbes, in partnership with Statista, also named Brock one of Canada’s Top Employers for Company Culture. At Brock, you will find a welcoming, inclusive community and an exciting range of meaningful career opportunities. Ignite new possibilities for your career. Break through at Brock. Post End Date: October 9, 2026 at 11:59 PM This job advertisement is to fill an existing vacancy in the Administrative Professional (Employee Group) About the Role:     Reporting to the Associate Vice-President, Alumni and Development , the Administrative Coordinator provides comprehensive administrative and coordination support for the Associate Vice-President, Alumni & Development. The Administrative Coordinator ensures smooth delivery of operations, and departmental processes, while maintaining compliance with institutional policies, procedures, processes and timelines. They acts as a key resource for the AVP and leadership team by coordinating administrative activities, managing information and communications, supporting meetings and committees, monitoring follow-up activities, and facilitating effective coordination with internal and external stakeholders.    The Administrative Coordinator will:    Serve as the first point of contact for internal and external stakeholders, responding to inquiries, processing requests, and facilitating communication with the AVP;  Monitor the AVP's email account, distributing messages as needed and coordinating responses on behalf of the Office;  Review incoming materials and requests, including confidential matters, and note information requiring follow-up;  Coordinate and process requests requiring the AVP's review, approval, or signature;  Maintain records, filing systems, tracking tools, and databases in accordance with university policies, privacy requirements, and confidentiality standards;  Act as a liaison between Alumni & Development, Advancement units, and other University departments to facilitate effective communication and administrative support;  Maintain positive, collaborative relationships with campus and external partners, including volunteers, alumni and donors, to ensure excellent customer service;  Liaise with other Alumni and Development leadership offices and University departments as needed regarding Alumni & Development activities to ensure awareness and appropriate coordination;  Administer and prioritize the AVP's schedule, coordinating meetings and engagement opportunities while balancing competing priorities;  Schedule and coordinate meetings for the AVP and leadership team, including aligning participant schedules, arranging logistics, and ensuring necessary preparation requirements are addressed;  Prepare and assemble briefing materials, reports, correspondence, and supporting documentation for meetings and stakeholder engagements;  Maintain the accuracy and integrity of database records through data entry, updates, tracking, and reporting activities in accordance with privacy requirements;    Key Skills and Experience:   College Diploma in related discipline or the equivalent combination of education and experience.  Knowledge of office administration concepts, practices and techniques;  Knowledge of the administrative functions and governance structures within a university advancement or development environment;  Knowledge of University processes and policies;  Familiarity with the fundraising cycle, donor stewardship principles, and advancement services processes;  Solid understanding of budget development, financial record keeping and reporting;   Strong computer skills, including advanced knowledge of Microsoft Office, SharePoint, Workday, and donor database/CRM systems (e.g., Raiser's Edge);  Ability to work effectively with confidential and sensitive donor, alumni and prospect information, exercising tact, diplomacy and discretion;  Excellent communication skills, including concise and accurate writing proficiency, editing and proofreading skills, and the ability to professionally interact with all levels of contacts;  Ability to balance and anticipate the needs of an executive and/or division with the needs of the organization.     Preferred or Asset Skills:    Undergraduate degree, Experience working with a donor or alumni database/CRM (such as Raiser's Edge or a similar advancement platform); and   Experience supporting a senior leader in a fundraising, alumni relations, or non-profit development environment.  Salary and Total Rewards:    Job Grade [I], Salary Scale ($52,000 - $84,000);  Target Hiring Range: $60,000 – $65,000   This is a fixed Term Contract Position for up to 12 months with;   Health & Dental Benefits:  Comprehensive extended health, dental, and vision coverage.  Pension Plan:  Enrollment eligibility in the Brock University Pension Plan.  Vacation:  Up to 3 weeks per year, in addition to university holidays.  Professional Development:  Eligibility for the Brock Tuition Waiver Program.  *The final salary is based on experience, internal equity, and budget considerations within the target hiring range. We are committed to offering flexible work arrangements where possible as outlined in our Flexible Work Arrangement Policy . As a student-centered organization, all employees are required to work on campus as needed.   Brock University is committed to creating a respectful and equitable workplace. We strive to foster a culture of diversity and inclusion in our work and learning environments. We welcome applications from all qualified individuals and actively encourage applications from women, people with disabilities, members of the 2SLGBTQIA+ community, Indigenous Peoples, people who identify as Black, African and/or Caribbean, as racialized and/or as from ethnic and cultural minority groups, and other underrepresented demographic groups at Brock and in the Niagara region. Brock also recognizes intersectionality and the interconnected identities, histories, and experiences of these aforementioned groups .   We are committed to inclusive and barrier-free recruitment, and we accommodat e the needs of applicants throughout all stages of the recruitment process, as outlined in our Employment Accommodation Policy and consistent with the requirements of the Ontario Human Rights Code . Please contact talent@brocku.ca   if you require a disability related accommodation so we can ensure you r participation needs are met.   Brock University does not use AI Technology at any stage of the recruitment process.   We appreciate all applications received . C andidates that are selected for an interview will be contacted.   Learn more about Brock University by visiting www.brocku.ca ."
